WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.842
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:07.112 --> 00:09.114
[theme music playing]

3
00:30.594 --> 00:32.346
LOS ANGELES, 2001

4
00:32.429 --> 00:35.099
[upbeat music playing]

5
00:51.323 --> 00:53.993
How much longer on the chilled octopus salad for Table 5?

6
00:55.578 --> 00:58.622
-Two minutes, Chef. -The octopus is smaller than usual today.

7
00:58.706 --> 00:59.999
Remove it 30 seconds early.

8
01:00.082 --> 01:02.376
-Don't forget to drizzle the perilla oil. -Yes, Chef.

9
01:07.006 --> 01:09.633
For Table 2, royal-style stir-fried beef and vegetables.

10
01:10.968 --> 01:15.097
Table 3 says it's too spicy and wants it a little milder, Chef. Sir.

11
01:15.180 --> 01:17.641
So much for saying they could handle spicy food.

12
01:17.725 --> 01:19.351
Chef. Table 2 changed their order.

13
01:19.435 --> 01:21.228
Two galbijjim instead of pork bossam.

14
01:22.396 --> 01:25.441
Okay, guys. We have two beef galbijjim for table number two.

15
01:25.524 --> 01:26.525
-Yes, Chef. -Yes, Chef.

16
01:27.109 --> 01:28.861
-Uh, one more thing, Chef. -Hmm?

17
01:29.445 --> 01:30.613
Someone is here to see you.

18
01:31.196 --> 01:32.406
-Me? -Yeah.

19
01:36.452 --> 01:38.412
Who is it? What do they look like?

20
01:38.495 --> 01:40.080
Uh, I've never seen her before.

21
01:40.164 --> 01:41.999
A young Korean woman. [inhales sharply]

22
01:42.082 --> 01:43.834
She had rather delicate features.

23
01:45.920 --> 01:47.379
She's at Table 5.

24
01:52.176 --> 01:54.219
[mysterious music playing]

25
02:02.686 --> 02:04.355
Excuse me?

26
02:13.864 --> 02:14.865
[gasps softly]

27
02:18.243 --> 02:19.411
[gasps softly]

28
02:20.037 --> 02:21.872
Je… Jeong-suk.

29
02:31.382 --> 02:32.383
[sniffles]

30
02:38.013 --> 02:39.014
[sniffles]

31
02:40.432 --> 02:41.850
Dad.

32
02:42.434 --> 02:43.811
[gasps]

33
02:44.895 --> 02:46.271
Han.

34
02:52.778 --> 02:55.280
[shudders] Han. [sobs]

35
02:58.492 --> 02:59.785
[Jeong-suk] Who is he?

36
03:02.371 --> 03:03.372
Cheonghyang.

37
03:04.665 --> 03:06.959
You said your father told you about cheonghyang.

38
03:09.837 --> 03:10.838
Who is he?

39
03:17.761 --> 03:18.762
Chris.

40
03:18.846 --> 03:20.556
[inhales deeply]

41
03:21.390 --> 03:22.391
What's going on?

42
03:23.642 --> 03:25.978
What brings you two here at this hour?

43
03:26.562 --> 03:28.689
I doubt you came to see Song-yi and me.

44
03:29.606 --> 03:30.816
Or do you need…

45
03:33.193 --> 03:34.778
some B-roll footage for this too?

46
03:35.612 --> 03:37.239
No, that's not it.

47
03:38.240 --> 03:40.868
We came to deliver an invitation to Mr. Park.

48
03:40.951 --> 03:43.245
We have been delivering invitations

49
03:43.954 --> 03:47.583
to every brewery in Haeon County for the live show.

50
03:47.666 --> 03:51.378
We're hoping all of Haeon's traditional liquor artisans

51
03:51.462 --> 03:54.131
will attend and honor us with their presence.

52
03:58.969 --> 03:59.970
[inhales deeply]

53
04:00.596 --> 04:02.306
Looks like we're in your way.

54
04:07.811 --> 04:09.396
Thank you so much for the drink, sir.

55
04:12.733 --> 04:14.485
We'll leave you three to talk.

56
04:37.591 --> 04:39.009
Still haven't given up on it?

57
04:42.763 --> 04:44.890
It's become a thing of the past.

58
04:45.641 --> 04:47.142
What do you want with it?

59
04:47.851 --> 04:49.770
You're still misunderstanding me.

60
04:51.313 --> 04:55.567
I never… I never told you that you should give up on Jehyangju.

61
05:00.030 --> 05:01.031
Listen.

62
05:03.450 --> 05:04.493
Jehyangju

63
05:05.536 --> 05:09.123
is a clear rice wine made with local rice and traditional nuruk.

64
05:09.998 --> 05:12.126
And the water has to come from Mount Gyesul.

65
05:12.709 --> 05:14.044
Listen, sir.

66
05:14.128 --> 05:16.880
I'm not saying you should stop making cheongju.

67
05:17.381 --> 05:19.466
I'm saying you should take a more practical, business-orient--

68
05:19.550 --> 05:21.718
Enough! That's enough!

69
05:23.470 --> 05:26.974
All this talk about business and global markets, that's enough!

70
05:30.185 --> 05:31.353
I'm really sorry.

71
05:34.731 --> 05:35.941
I know that too.

72
05:36.900 --> 05:40.112
I know cheongju is dismissed as an imitation of Japanese sake.

73
05:41.488 --> 05:44.283
No matter how faithfully we try using traditional methods,

74
05:44.366 --> 05:45.367
in the end…

75
05:58.964 --> 05:59.965
[exhales sharply]

76
06:10.058 --> 06:11.685
That is all that's left.

77
06:14.980 --> 06:16.899
It's time to let it go now.

78
06:19.276 --> 06:21.153
Let it fade away with dignity.

79
06:37.127 --> 06:38.754
[breathes deeply]

80
06:45.886 --> 06:48.222
Slow down a little, Chris!

81
06:50.265 --> 06:51.266
[Han sighs]

82
06:54.978 --> 06:56.605
Can't you tell me what's going on?

83
06:56.688 --> 06:58.023
What do you mean?

84
06:58.106 --> 07:00.692
You haven't said a word the whole way here.

85
07:00.776 --> 07:03.070
Not since we ran into Judge Yoon Jeong-suk.

86
07:04.655 --> 07:06.990
Did the two of you already know each other?

87
07:07.574 --> 07:10.244
Why was she asking you about your father?

88
07:10.327 --> 07:11.912
[sighs]

89
07:14.039 --> 07:15.499
-Chris. -Song.

90
07:16.083 --> 07:18.168
Let's just hurry back. We have a lot of work to do.

91
07:19.670 --> 07:21.213
Tell me, what is going on?

92
07:21.296 --> 07:23.131
What is it that you're hiding?

93
07:25.092 --> 07:26.134
Chris.

94
07:27.177 --> 07:28.804
I want to know. Please tell me.

95
07:28.887 --> 07:30.806
[breathes deeply]

96
07:30.889 --> 07:32.474
Tell me, Chris.

97
07:35.102 --> 07:36.812
-Chris! -Song, enough!

98
07:46.530 --> 07:47.948
Why do you want to know?

99
07:49.658 --> 07:51.201
Because I've been worried.

100
07:53.620 --> 07:55.539
I'm worried about you, Chris.

101
07:57.124 --> 08:00.335
You didn't tell me anything the day you collapsed, or even the day after.

102
08:00.419 --> 08:03.463
Anyone who saw you could tell it wasn't just anemia like you said.

103
08:05.799 --> 08:09.720
Also, as to why you changed your mind and entered this competition,

104
08:09.803 --> 08:13.223
even though it meant violating your contract and having to pay a fine…

105
08:13.890 --> 08:15.434
You still haven't answered any of that.

106
08:19.855 --> 08:20.981
Chris.

107
08:22.149 --> 08:23.358
I want to know.

108
08:24.568 --> 08:26.695
I want to be of some help to you too.

109
08:30.699 --> 08:32.242
Tell me, Chris.

110
08:34.286 --> 08:35.287
[Han sighs]

111
08:36.496 --> 08:38.040
[Han] Not yet.

112
08:38.749 --> 08:40.042
It's not time yet.

113
08:44.796 --> 08:46.173
Chris.

114
08:48.300 --> 08:49.760
[gasping]

115
08:55.349 --> 08:56.725
[Song-yi screams]

116
09:24.044 --> 09:26.505
[gentle music playing]

117
09:40.936 --> 09:42.646
Did you sleep well?

118
09:46.942 --> 09:48.443
Please take me to him!

119
09:49.027 --> 09:51.613
Just let me see him once. [crying]

120
09:51.696 --> 09:54.366
Take me to my dad, please.

121
09:55.700 --> 09:56.910
Just once!

122
09:59.746 --> 10:01.706
[boiling]

123
10:01.790 --> 10:03.542
[lid rattling]

124
10:30.402 --> 10:31.403
What is that?

125
10:35.949 --> 10:37.117
It's red onion tea.

126
10:38.452 --> 10:40.412
It should warm you up a little bit.

127
10:41.204 --> 10:42.205
Onion tea?

128
10:42.706 --> 10:43.999
You can make tea with onions?

129
10:44.082 --> 10:46.126
It's good for preventing colds.

130
10:46.209 --> 10:48.336
My father often made it for me when I was little.

131
10:55.427 --> 10:56.428
How is it?

132
10:57.554 --> 11:00.182
It's good. I feel more relaxed already.

133
11:00.265 --> 11:01.975
[chuckles softly]

134
11:08.482 --> 11:09.566
I'm sorry…

135
11:11.526 --> 11:12.527
for

136
11:13.361 --> 11:15.280
pushing you so hard.

137
11:20.368 --> 11:21.369
Chris.

138
11:23.830 --> 11:25.790
Nothing else matters to me.

139
11:25.874 --> 11:27.876
I don't care what your reasons are.

140
11:29.377 --> 11:30.378
Because

141
11:31.129 --> 11:33.924
you are what matters most to me, Chris.

142
11:35.675 --> 11:37.260
Whatever happens,

143
11:39.095 --> 11:40.639
I believe in you, Chris.

144
11:42.265 --> 11:44.267
In Team Famiglia's captain.

145
12:03.995 --> 12:04.996
Oh.

146
12:06.957 --> 12:10.168
Where did I put my pants?

147
12:10.252 --> 12:12.629
You asked me to put them in the washing machine with mine.

148
12:12.712 --> 12:14.172
-Huh? -What?

149
12:14.256 --> 12:15.257
The talisman.

150
12:15.799 --> 12:17.676
My talisman! [gasping]

151
12:18.802 --> 12:19.803
"Talisman"?

152
12:21.429 --> 12:23.098
-[gasping] Oh, no! -Song!

153
12:23.932 --> 12:26.685
No! My talisman. I have to get it out.

154
12:26.768 --> 12:28.853
-It can't get ruined. -What?

155
12:28.937 --> 12:29.938
Are you out of your mind?

156
12:30.021 --> 12:31.815
You'll break it. The water's going to spill everywhere!

157
12:31.898 --> 12:34.609
I have to get it out right now. I really can't be without it.

158
12:35.527 --> 12:36.778
-[yelps] -No, you have to wait!

159
12:36.861 --> 12:38.071
Take it easy, okay?

160
12:38.154 --> 12:40.699
No! No. [whining]

161
12:40.782 --> 12:42.534
No!

162
12:43.326 --> 12:45.620
[crying] No!

163
13:05.890 --> 13:08.476
[wails]

164
13:09.352 --> 13:11.521
[crying]

165
13:12.647 --> 13:13.940
What do you mean?

166
13:14.024 --> 13:15.817
He's replacing a team member?

167
13:15.900 --> 13:18.528
[sighs] I've been taken aback too, ma'am.

168
13:18.612 --> 13:20.238
I thought he was joking at first.

169
13:21.072 --> 13:22.824
[sighs, scoffs]

170
13:23.700 --> 13:24.951
Does he think TV's a joke?

171
13:25.035 --> 13:27.120
What's his reason? Did you ask Chef Cha Woo-jin?

172
13:27.704 --> 13:28.872
Apparently,

173
13:28.955 --> 13:32.500
Chef Bae Yeong-su himself asked the writers to replace him.

174
13:32.584 --> 13:34.753
-He said he's lost confidence. -What?

175
13:34.836 --> 13:38.423
He must have been really on edge. And under a lot of pressure too.

176
13:39.007 --> 13:40.216
[sighs]

177
13:41.926 --> 13:43.261
So who's replacing him?

178
13:43.345 --> 13:46.222
As we speak, Chef Michael Jang is on his way.

179
13:48.516 --> 13:50.018
What should we do?

180
13:50.101 --> 13:53.104
I guess there's nothing we can do. He asked to be replaced, after all.

181
13:53.855 --> 13:55.982
Besides, we let Team Hush recruit Chef Isabel

182
13:56.066 --> 13:58.568
even though she wasn't originally on their team.

183
13:58.652 --> 13:59.653
Right.

184
14:00.737 --> 14:02.113
[Hyeon-ju] Ms. Seon!

185
14:06.076 --> 14:07.702
-You can go. -Uh-huh.

186
14:11.081 --> 14:14.250
Everything going well? Any… Any difficulties?

187
14:14.834 --> 14:16.169
Oh, no. Everything's fine, ma'am.

188
14:16.252 --> 14:18.171
Mmm. Good.

189
14:18.963 --> 14:20.090
Wow.

190
14:21.591 --> 14:23.009
This is nice.

191
14:24.844 --> 14:27.222
Um, is there something you wanted to say?

192
14:27.305 --> 14:28.390
Hmm?

193
14:28.473 --> 14:31.309
Oh, uh, well… No. [chuckles] Not really.

194
14:32.560 --> 14:34.270
Oh! Over here, Director Choi.

195
14:37.816 --> 14:40.276
-Oh. There you are, Ms. Baek. -[chuckles]

196
14:41.444 --> 14:42.445
Say hello.

197
14:42.529 --> 14:44.781
You know him, right? Director Choi Sang-hyeon.

198
14:45.448 --> 14:47.450
Uh, yes.

199
14:48.493 --> 14:50.286
Long time no see, Ms. Seon.

200
14:50.370 --> 14:51.371
Been well?

201
14:51.955 --> 14:54.582
Yes, of course. It's been a while, Sang-hyeon.

202
14:54.666 --> 14:55.834
Hmm.

203
14:56.751 --> 14:58.169
So what brings you here?

204
14:58.753 --> 15:01.756
Oh, I called him over. For tomorrow's live broadcast.

205
15:01.840 --> 15:03.675
-Huh? -Come on, Ms. Seon.

206
15:03.758 --> 15:06.177
It's been ages since you've directed a live broadcast.

207
15:06.261 --> 15:08.555
But Director Choi here specializes in

208
15:09.431 --> 15:11.266
-live broadcasts. -Oh, no.

209
15:12.684 --> 15:14.561
[both chuckling]

210
15:17.063 --> 15:19.315
What do you mean they'll handle the live broadcast?

211
15:19.983 --> 15:22.068
I thought they were here as our backup.

212
15:22.152 --> 15:24.529
Yes, but I told them to handle it while they're here.

213
15:24.612 --> 15:27.824
[inhales sharply] Ms. Seon, you have tomorrow's episode to edit

214
15:27.907 --> 15:29.617
and the live broadcast to prepare for.

215
15:29.701 --> 15:31.119
You're completely swamped as it is,

216
15:31.202 --> 15:33.621
and you want to direct the live show? [gasps]

217
15:33.705 --> 15:35.582
That's way too much.

218
15:35.665 --> 15:37.667
You should sit in the audience with the producers

219
15:37.751 --> 15:39.377
and just enjoy the show tomorrow.

220
15:39.878 --> 15:42.088
Director Choi is a live-broadcast expert.

221
15:42.589 --> 15:43.715
Just trust him.

222
15:43.798 --> 15:45.508
And let him do his job!

223
15:45.592 --> 15:48.470
You can't do this without speaking to me first.

224
15:48.553 --> 15:51.806
I am the chief producer of this show.

225
15:52.432 --> 15:55.143
How can you make a decision like this without even consulting me?

226
15:55.226 --> 15:56.394
Ms. Seon.

227
15:56.478 --> 15:59.898
I told you I'd send down a support team, didn't I?

228
15:59.981 --> 16:01.858
This is all being done for you.

229
16:01.941 --> 16:03.109
Stop this.

230
16:03.193 --> 16:06.362
You know very well this isn't for me or my team.

231
16:06.446 --> 16:08.782
And it definitely isn't for the show.

232
16:09.532 --> 16:11.826
I can't hand this over to someone else.

233
16:11.910 --> 16:13.036
What?

234
16:13.119 --> 16:16.539
Again, the director of this show is me.

235
16:17.499 --> 16:19.584
I'll direct the live broadcast as planned,

236
16:20.668 --> 16:21.669
Ms. Baek.

237
16:27.091 --> 16:28.092
Jeong-won.

238
16:36.559 --> 16:39.896
I think that you've got it all wrong here.

239
16:39.979 --> 16:44.859
I'm the one who decides the director of this show, not you, do you understand?

240
16:50.323 --> 16:52.408
I think the fact that…

241
16:53.243 --> 16:55.912
Chairwoman Moon favors you has gone to your head.

242
16:57.121 --> 16:58.248
Is that it?

243
16:59.457 --> 17:00.458
Huh?

244
17:02.085 --> 17:04.963
What? Another team's doing the broadcast?

245
17:08.299 --> 17:10.510
[sighs deeply]

246
17:10.593 --> 17:12.303
I don't know what to say.

247
17:12.387 --> 17:13.471
-Wait a minute. -[sighs]

248
17:13.555 --> 17:15.640
What kind of nonsense is this, huh?

249
17:15.723 --> 17:17.517
We hand over the script we wrote

250
17:17.600 --> 17:19.936
just so a different team can run the live show?

251
17:20.562 --> 17:22.605
Ugh, this is TV, not some kids' game.

252
17:24.315 --> 17:28.403
Then do you think you can work with the team that arrived today, Ms. Seon?

253
17:28.486 --> 17:29.487
[sighs]

254
17:30.822 --> 17:32.448
I won't be directing.

255
17:33.908 --> 17:36.870
Ms. Baek brought in a freelance director to take over.

256
17:36.953 --> 17:38.204
Choi Sang-hyeon.

257
17:39.747 --> 17:42.959
What now? That Choi Sang-hyeon? [sighs]

258
17:43.042 --> 17:46.170
-[Hyeon-ju shouting] Damn it. -[thudding]

259
17:46.254 --> 17:48.590
[object clattering, shattering]

260
17:48.673 --> 17:50.633
-[Hyeong-koo grunts] -[Hyeon-ju panting]

261
17:52.719 --> 17:54.512
Damn it. [panting]

262
18:00.852 --> 18:02.270
I don't believe it.

263
18:02.353 --> 18:05.148
Now all these nobodies think they can challenge me now?

264
18:05.231 --> 18:06.649
[screams]

265
18:07.901 --> 18:09.861
If I had my way, I'd just--

266
18:09.944 --> 18:11.779
[snoring]

267
18:11.863 --> 18:13.114
What?

268
18:13.197 --> 18:14.616
Are you snoring?

269
18:15.283 --> 18:16.868
You fell asleep?

270
18:18.244 --> 18:19.245
Get out of there.

271
18:19.913 --> 18:20.914
Okay.

272
18:20.997 --> 18:23.207
-Come on! Get out of there! -Yes, ma'am.

273
18:25.418 --> 18:27.003
[coughs]

274
18:27.879 --> 18:29.464
-You're okay, right? -Yes.

275
18:29.547 --> 18:31.090
Nothing hurts, right?

276
18:31.174 --> 18:33.885
N-No. I'm fine. Nothing hurts, Ms. Baek.

277
18:35.053 --> 18:37.055
We're leaving in ten minutes. So go get ready.

278
18:37.138 --> 18:38.139
Yes, ma'am.

279
18:38.222 --> 18:40.850
Call housekeeping and have the room cleaned up! Hurry!

280
18:40.934 --> 18:42.310
Yes, Ms. Baek.

281
18:42.393 --> 18:44.103
-Koo! -At your service.

282
18:44.187 --> 18:45.647
Pick up what's yours.

283
18:45.730 --> 18:47.106
No one's gonna do it for you.

284
18:47.190 --> 18:52.028
[chuckles] Right. My apologies. I was a bit out of it. Apologies.

285
18:52.111 --> 18:54.364
I'll take it with me. [grunts]

286
18:56.616 --> 18:57.617
[sighs]

287
18:58.326 --> 19:01.162
My blood's boiling. Ugh, I'm pissed! Ow!

288
19:01.245 --> 19:03.081
[panting]

289
19:04.749 --> 19:05.917
[sighs loudly]

290
19:07.001 --> 19:09.462
[exhales] Refreshing.

291
19:10.838 --> 19:13.049
[tense music playing]

292
19:16.052 --> 19:17.053
Nice.

293
19:17.762 --> 19:18.763
Very nice.

294
19:19.681 --> 19:21.265
[sucks teeth] Good work, Jeon.

295
19:21.349 --> 19:22.809
You really put in a lot of effort this time.

296
19:22.892 --> 19:24.227
Thank you, Ms. Baek.

297
19:24.852 --> 19:27.105
I'm counting on you, Director Choi.

298
19:27.772 --> 19:29.732
Let's… [inhales sharply] …put on a great show.

299
19:30.441 --> 19:31.567
Don't worry, Ms. Baek.

300
19:31.651 --> 19:34.237
-I'm going to make it look incredible. -Good.

301
19:34.320 --> 19:35.321
Okay.

302
19:35.822 --> 19:36.823
[gasps]

303
19:37.740 --> 19:39.534
[exhales, shudders]

304
19:39.617 --> 19:40.618
[shivers]

305
19:40.702 --> 19:42.912
-This is bad. -Huh?

306
19:44.580 --> 19:47.583
I'm just so excited about this.

307
19:47.667 --> 19:50.169
-I'm just so excited, I can't wait. -Yeah.

308
19:50.253 --> 19:52.130
Oh, my goodness. [breathing heavily]

309
19:52.213 --> 19:54.424
I can't wait. I think this is going to be so much fun.

310
19:54.507 --> 19:57.218
[shouting] Oh, I can't wait! [cackles]

311
19:58.428 --> 20:00.555
[cackling]

312
20:02.223 --> 20:04.475
Wait. Where do we go from here?

313
20:04.559 --> 20:06.394
Don't we have to cross the road here?

314
20:06.477 --> 20:09.105
That way? No, no, no. It's this way.

315
20:09.689 --> 20:11.315
-This is it. Yeah. -Oh, is it?

316
20:12.900 --> 20:15.528
FORTUNES, NAMING, LOVE, MARRIAGE, PROPERTY

317
20:19.365 --> 20:21.242
-Oh, Young Master Yangbok. -We found it.

318
20:22.493 --> 20:23.870
VACATION AUGUST 20-24

319
20:24.454 --> 20:25.455
[gasps]

320
20:27.123 --> 20:29.792
Oh… [clicks tongue] Come on.

321
20:30.877 --> 20:32.837
He's on vacation? Until when?

322
20:34.213 --> 20:37.508
[sighs] This is driving me crazy. Why now?

323
20:38.134 --> 20:39.135
I'm here.

324
20:40.136 --> 20:41.804
I guess there's nothing we can do.

325
20:42.680 --> 20:43.848
No.

326
20:43.931 --> 20:47.894
We need someone who knows the full story to draw a talisman that works.

327
20:49.353 --> 20:50.354
Yes, Auntie.

328
20:51.606 --> 20:53.608
Okay. Thanks for trying.

329
20:56.110 --> 20:57.111
[phone beeps]

330
20:58.321 --> 21:02.158
Ugh! Why did I have to ask him to put it in the washing machine?

331
21:02.241 --> 21:04.911
[sighs] What should I do now?

332
21:04.994 --> 21:06.662
I don't want anyone getting hurt.

333
21:10.792 --> 21:12.460
[mischievous music playing]

334
21:14.670 --> 21:16.005
Um, excuse me.

335
21:17.673 --> 21:21.260
Do you have to keep following me around?

336
21:23.763 --> 21:26.808
Well, the thing is, we don't have much outdoor footage.

337
21:27.391 --> 21:30.103
So whenever someone leaves the training center,

338
21:30.186 --> 21:32.814
we try to follow them around and film a bit.

339
21:33.481 --> 21:34.482
Oh, dear.

340
21:35.441 --> 21:37.318
Uh, you see,

341
21:37.401 --> 21:42.949
I have a very important, very private, personal appointment right now.

342
21:43.449 --> 21:46.160
Could you maybe film me in an hour or two instead?

343
21:46.244 --> 21:48.412
Oh! I'll call you when I'm done.

344
21:48.496 --> 21:50.498
Why don't you go get something cold to drink for now?

345
21:50.581 --> 21:51.624
Huh?

346
21:51.707 --> 21:53.251
Please go. [chuckles]

347
21:53.334 --> 21:54.585
No, wait. Hold on.

348
21:57.922 --> 22:00.424
You want a what? A talisman?

349
22:00.508 --> 22:01.592
Listen, sweetie.

350
22:02.468 --> 22:04.220
A talisman is not going to cut it.

351
22:04.303 --> 22:07.598
You've got a nasty-tempered one sitting on top of your head,

352
22:07.682 --> 22:08.850
and you want a talisman?

353
22:08.933 --> 22:11.435
I'm afraid that won't help at all.

354
22:12.270 --> 22:15.148
Yes, I was told that before, but I'm…

355
22:16.274 --> 22:18.025
just really desperate.

356
22:19.527 --> 22:20.570
Let's hold a rite, then.

357
22:21.696 --> 22:24.448
I think 20 million won should do.

358
22:26.284 --> 22:27.410
[shaman] By tomorrow?

359
22:27.493 --> 22:29.287
I can't do that overnight.

360
22:29.370 --> 22:31.539
Drawing a talisman is no child's play.

361
22:33.833 --> 22:35.126
If you're really that desperate,

362
22:35.835 --> 22:38.671
look, you can pick one from the library. Take a look.

363
22:40.006 --> 22:41.007
What?

364
22:41.090 --> 22:42.633
There's a library for talismans too?

365
22:42.717 --> 22:45.303
Of course. I've got every kind here.

366
22:45.386 --> 22:47.680
Just pick one, and I can draw it in one hour.

367
22:47.763 --> 22:49.056
Look here.

368
22:49.140 --> 22:51.309
Marriage, right? Love.

369
22:51.392 --> 22:54.812
And here. Yes, wealth, promotion…

370
22:54.896 --> 22:58.482
Let's see now. I think you need a misfortune-transferring talisman.

371
22:58.566 --> 23:02.236
Where was that again? Misfortune-transfer…

372
23:02.320 --> 23:03.321
Where's the M tab?

373
23:11.329 --> 23:14.207
Okay, let me see.

374
23:14.290 --> 23:18.961
Weave three lines together on the left, then bend them this way…

375
23:21.297 --> 23:23.007
You see… [chuckles]

376
23:23.090 --> 23:26.135
I actually used to work at a securities firm.

377
23:26.719 --> 23:28.512
I only recently became a shaman.

378
23:28.596 --> 23:31.474
-I haven't drawn very many talismans yet. -What?

379
23:31.557 --> 23:32.642
I'm so sorry.

380
23:34.227 --> 23:35.603
You don't invest in stocks, do you?

381
23:35.686 --> 23:37.313
[whimsical music playing]

382
23:37.396 --> 23:39.482
MISFORTUNE-REPELLING TALISMAN

383
23:42.818 --> 23:45.655
These days, AI does it all for you.

384
23:45.738 --> 23:46.739
[chuckles]

385
24:02.421 --> 24:04.632
Geez. [grunts]

386
24:06.133 --> 24:08.094
Oh! Hello.

387
24:10.221 --> 24:11.389
Oh, hello.

388
24:13.307 --> 24:17.687
Most of these materials, aside from the books, haven't been digitized,

389
24:17.770 --> 24:19.897
so you probably won't find them anywhere else.

390
24:19.981 --> 24:21.274
Oh, I see.

391
24:21.357 --> 24:22.775
Take your time.

392
24:22.858 --> 24:26.612
Oh, and these materials are extremely valuable,

393
24:26.696 --> 24:29.365
so we can't let you borrow them, but you're welcome to take photos though.

394
24:29.448 --> 24:31.450
-Oh, okay. I understand. -All right.

395
24:31.534 --> 24:32.743
-Thank you. -No problem.

396
24:45.840 --> 24:47.425
"WHEN A TYPE OF LIQUOR DISAPPEARS,

397
24:47.508 --> 24:48.718
WE LOSE A PAGE OF HISTORY"

398
24:48.801 --> 24:51.595
"It is made only with water from Mount Gyesul,

399
24:51.679 --> 24:53.973
rice and handmade traditional nuruk."

400
24:55.891 --> 24:59.937
"He revived a native rice variety lost during the Japanese colonial period

401
25:00.021 --> 25:01.355
and used it to brew Jehyangju…"

402
25:01.439 --> 25:04.150
"Dedicated his entire life to brewing cheongju."

403
25:04.233 --> 25:07.236
"The only person in Haeon still carrying the tradition of cheongju…"

404
25:07.320 --> 25:10.031
"Stopped production last winter and relinquished his status

405
25:10.114 --> 25:13.576
as a Certified Holder of South Gyeongsang's Cultural Heritage."

406
25:13.659 --> 25:14.660
Ah.

407
25:14.744 --> 25:17.079
So this is why he doesn't make it anymore.

408
25:17.163 --> 25:18.164
Hmm.

409
25:21.876 --> 25:23.210
TRADITIONAL LIQUOR, REDESIGNED

410
25:26.422 --> 25:27.590
Distilled liquor.

411
25:27.673 --> 25:30.384
"Distilled liquor production began during the Goryeo era,

412
25:30.468 --> 25:33.554
when distillation techniques were introduced from the Yuan Dynasty…"

413
25:33.637 --> 25:35.765
"Soju breweries in Andong and Jeju,

414
25:35.848 --> 25:39.185
which served as forward bases for military campaigns against Japan…"

415
25:39.268 --> 25:41.103
"Cheongju, a clear rice wine,

416
25:41.187 --> 25:45.232
is made with just three main ingredients rather than adding more ingredients,

417
25:45.316 --> 25:48.069
producing a deep, subtle aroma and a clean taste…"

418
25:52.907 --> 25:57.036
"As brewing methods were passed down through families during the Joseon era,

419
25:57.119 --> 26:00.164
the age of home-brewed liquor truly blossomed…"

420
26:00.247 --> 26:03.876
"When home brewing was banned during the Japanese colonial period,

421
26:03.959 --> 26:06.962
countless traditional liquors faded into history…"

422
26:07.046 --> 26:09.590
"Authentic cheongju must be made exclusively

423
26:09.673 --> 26:12.009
from rice, water and traditional nuruk."

424
26:12.093 --> 26:14.136
"And it must be aged for a certain period

425
26:14.220 --> 26:17.181
to develop its distinctive clean, delicate taste and aroma…"

426
26:17.890 --> 26:21.102
"Water, rice… traditional nuruk."

427
26:22.061 --> 26:23.938
"Must be aged for a certain period."

428
26:31.320 --> 26:33.197
[shutter clicks]

429
26:33.280 --> 26:34.865
And this…

430
26:46.419 --> 26:47.837
[phone buzzing]

431
26:47.920 --> 26:49.713
THE TABLE CAMERA OPERATOR KIM HYEONG-JUN

432
26:50.798 --> 26:53.467
-[inhales sharply] Ah, yes, hello? -[Hyeong-Jun] Ah, yes, Chef.

433
26:53.551 --> 26:56.011
I'm outside the traditional liquor museum you mentioned.

434
26:56.095 --> 26:57.096
Oh, okay.

435
26:57.179 --> 27:00.391
Please go ahead and come into the building then head straight to the archive room.

436
27:00.474 --> 27:02.184
Uh, but, uh…

437
27:02.268 --> 27:05.354
we need to get a shot of you coming in through the main entrance.

438
27:05.438 --> 27:09.024
Sorry to trouble you, but could you come out to the main entrance real quick?

439
27:09.108 --> 27:11.861
A shot of me coming in through the main entrance?

440
27:11.944 --> 27:13.154
Yes, yes, yes.

441
27:13.237 --> 27:16.699
So it looks like you're visiting the museum for the first time.

442
27:16.782 --> 27:18.325
That's just how TV works. [laughs]

443
27:18.409 --> 27:21.120
Ah. Okay, I understand.

444
27:21.203 --> 27:22.913
I'll make my way outside now.

445
27:23.831 --> 27:24.832
Okay.

446
27:25.332 --> 27:26.333
[phone beeps]

447
27:27.293 --> 27:31.672
[sighs] I guess filming for a TV show is pretty complicated work.

448
27:37.428 --> 27:38.596
YAKJU, 100, YAKJU

449
27:50.691 --> 27:52.401
YAKJU, 100, YAKJU

450
27:53.944 --> 27:55.613
[museum staff] It indicates the aging period.

451
27:56.197 --> 27:59.658
It's a display comparing liquor aged for over 100 days

452
27:59.742 --> 28:02.203
with liquor that hasn't been aged that long.

453
28:03.621 --> 28:08.417
Um, authentic cheongju needs to age for at least a hundred days after filtration.

454
28:08.501 --> 28:11.629
That's what gives it this distinctive pale-green hue.

455
28:12.213 --> 28:13.797
A hundred days…

456
28:17.801 --> 28:18.969
CANNOT ADDRESS HIS FATHER AS "FATHER"

457
28:19.929 --> 28:22.056
Cheongju is aged for

458
28:22.890 --> 28:23.974
a hundred days.

459
28:26.519 --> 28:29.897
But earlier, the label in that cabinet read,

460
28:29.980 --> 28:33.025
"yakju" next to the number 100, not "cheongju."

461
28:33.651 --> 28:35.611
Oh. That.

462
28:36.654 --> 28:38.656
Well, under the Liquor Tax Act,

463
28:38.739 --> 28:41.825
Korean-made rice wine isn't classified as cheongju.

464
28:41.909 --> 28:43.994
-What? -Um,

465
28:44.078 --> 28:46.622
only Japanese sake is classified as cheongju.

466
28:46.705 --> 28:49.291
Even when it's brewed using cheongju brewing methods,

467
28:49.375 --> 28:52.211
Korean-made rice wine is called yakju.

468
28:52.795 --> 28:54.380
I mean… But why?

469
28:54.463 --> 28:58.926
Then does that mean there's no traditional Korean cheongju?

470
28:59.593 --> 29:01.345
That's right. [clicks tongue]

471
29:01.428 --> 29:03.806
It's a shame, but that's the reality.

472
29:03.889 --> 29:05.891
No matter how good our cheongju is,

473
29:06.392 --> 29:09.520
we're not able to call our cheongju "cheongju."

474
29:31.750 --> 29:32.751
Thank you.

475
29:45.347 --> 29:47.766
CHEONGJU, RICE, NURUK, WATER

476
29:57.276 --> 30:01.655
"Only water, rice and nuruk. Rather than adding more…"

477
30:02.698 --> 30:04.408
Rather than adding more?

478
30:04.491 --> 30:07.077
Subtraction is greater than addition.

479
30:07.661 --> 30:09.079
Greater? More?

480
30:09.872 --> 30:12.750
There's more to take away than there is to add?

481
30:13.792 --> 30:16.211
Take away rather than add?

482
30:21.842 --> 30:23.802
100 days. [gasps]

483
30:23.886 --> 30:28.932
Um, authentic cheongju needs to age for at least a hundred days after filtration.

484
30:29.016 --> 30:31.518
That's what gives it this distinctive pale-green hue.

485
30:34.313 --> 30:37.358
"Cannot address his father as 'Father.'"

486
30:37.441 --> 30:40.152
Only Japanese sake is classified as cheongju.

487
30:40.235 --> 30:42.863
Even when it's brewed using cheongju brewing methods,

488
30:42.946 --> 30:45.449
Korean-made rice wine is called yakju.

489
30:45.532 --> 30:47.701
It's a shame, but that's the reality.

490
30:48.494 --> 30:50.496
No matter how good our cheongju is,

491
30:50.579 --> 30:53.832
we're not able to call our cheongju "cheongju."

492
30:56.335 --> 30:59.088
[Song-yi] We can't call our cheongju "cheongju."

493
31:00.255 --> 31:02.841
Cannot address his father as "Father."

494
31:06.345 --> 31:07.346
I found it.

495
31:18.315 --> 31:19.858
[grunts, sighs]

496
31:19.942 --> 31:21.193
I found it.

497
31:21.276 --> 31:23.404
[panting]

498
31:25.114 --> 31:26.990
The liquor for this challenge.

499
31:33.914 --> 31:37.584
If the liquor is cheongju, we need to rethink our approach.

500
31:38.127 --> 31:40.713
Do you think the other teams know it's cheongju?

501
31:41.964 --> 31:44.007
Should we tell them what we know?

502
31:45.592 --> 31:47.052
What if our guess is wrong?

503
31:47.136 --> 31:49.012
We'd have to take all the blame.

504
31:50.764 --> 31:54.435
Even if the liquor for the challenge is cheongju, there are dozens of varieties,

505
31:54.518 --> 31:56.061
each with subtle differences.

506
31:56.145 --> 31:58.439
It'll be a cheongju made here.

507
31:58.522 --> 32:02.943
One that pairs well with Haeon's local ingredients.

508
32:03.026 --> 32:06.363
Otherwise, there'd be no reason to bring us all the way out here.

509
32:06.447 --> 32:07.740
[sighs]

510
32:09.324 --> 32:11.785
Rice that's from here. Water from here.

511
32:13.245 --> 32:14.830
And a liquor that's made with

512
32:15.873 --> 32:17.583
wild nuruk cultivated here.

513
32:22.671 --> 32:24.631
Cheongju that carries Haeon's cheonghyang.

514
32:29.720 --> 32:30.721
Jehyangju.

515
32:32.306 --> 32:33.307
[chuckles]

516
32:34.767 --> 32:36.268
[clattering]

517
32:50.115 --> 32:51.366
[phone buzzing]

518
32:55.913 --> 32:57.456
NEW MESSAGE

519
32:57.539 --> 32:59.124
[Kim] We'll now reveal the main ingredients

520
32:59.208 --> 33:01.335
you'll be using for tomorrow's round.

521
33:01.418 --> 33:03.253
Head chefs, please gather

522
33:03.337 --> 33:06.131
at the Haeon Elementary School gym at midnight tonight.

523
33:09.384 --> 33:13.847
THE TABLE: K-CHEF 2026 MIDNIGHT, DAY OF ROUND 3

524
33:38.455 --> 33:39.873
[Jeong-won] All right, everyone's here.

525
34:03.063 --> 34:05.524
As I told you at the last shoot,

526
34:06.191 --> 34:09.361
the star of this challenge is the liquor.

527
34:11.613 --> 34:14.741
So you need to create a full spread centered on the liquor,

528
34:14.825 --> 34:16.577
not just snacks to go with it.

529
34:17.703 --> 34:19.705
All the ingredients in front of you

530
34:19.788 --> 34:22.291
were grown and raised right here in Haeon.

531
34:22.875 --> 34:24.418
Those of you who need to brine meat,

532
34:24.501 --> 34:27.921
prepare sauces in advance and let them sit overnight,

533
34:28.005 --> 34:30.591
or infuse oils with specific herbs,

534
34:31.174 --> 34:35.971
and those of you who want to cook ingredients sous vide in advance,

535
34:36.054 --> 34:39.766
please feel free to take whatever you need from the pantry in front of you.

536
34:39.850 --> 34:43.395
Tomorrow's round will be broadcast live.

537
34:43.478 --> 34:47.316
We can't predict what unexpected situations might arise.

538
34:47.399 --> 34:49.318
So please be sure to stay alert.

539
34:50.110 --> 34:51.570
I wish you all…

540
34:53.322 --> 34:54.531
the best of luck.

541
34:56.158 --> 34:59.703
[Hyeon-ju] Hae-seon. This is your first live appearance, isn't it?

542
34:59.786 --> 35:01.538
Thought you might be nervous.

543
35:01.622 --> 35:04.124
You can look forward to the show tomorrow.

544
35:04.207 --> 35:05.667
HERBAL RELAXANT

545
35:05.751 --> 35:07.794
SANGJU RICE

546
35:17.971 --> 35:20.223
Man, we need to know what the liquor is

547
35:20.307 --> 35:23.727
before we can decide what ingredients we need to take with us.

548
35:26.855 --> 35:29.441
Ms. Seon, how does framing on the main camera look?

549
35:30.108 --> 35:32.110
Go just a little wider.

550
35:33.654 --> 35:35.656
[Kim] Please go a little wider on the main camera.

551
36:12.234 --> 36:14.611
It's for lotus flower oil and pine needle oil.

552
36:15.195 --> 36:16.196
Song said

553
36:16.738 --> 36:19.658
Jehyangju has a lotus flower scent.

554
36:21.159 --> 36:22.703
The flavor and aroma

555
36:23.245 --> 36:24.746
reminded her of lotus flowers.

556
36:25.789 --> 36:27.416
Isn't this too much of a gamble?

557
36:29.001 --> 36:30.502
What if Jehyangju isn't the liquor?

558
36:31.461 --> 36:34.881
[sighs] And how can you be sure it smelled of lotus flowers?

559
36:34.965 --> 36:36.466
It will be.

560
36:37.050 --> 36:39.261
It's definitely going to be Jehyangju.

561
36:44.016 --> 36:45.767
[sighs]

562
36:50.564 --> 36:52.232
You really believe what that girl said?

563
36:53.525 --> 36:55.027
A lotus flower scent?

564
36:55.110 --> 36:57.738
Cheongju is made from rice without any additional ingredients.

565
36:57.821 --> 36:59.906
It's unlikely to have a specific aroma like that.

566
36:59.990 --> 37:01.408
-You know that too. -[sighs]

567
37:01.992 --> 37:04.953
Get a grip. Now's not the time to be swayed by a cooking novice.

568
37:08.457 --> 37:09.458
Chris.

569
37:10.042 --> 37:11.460
[sighs]

570
37:13.712 --> 37:15.213
I trust Song's instincts.

571
37:17.549 --> 37:18.550
[sighs]

572
37:21.428 --> 37:22.429
Do what you want.

573
37:29.436 --> 37:31.605
[grunting]

574
37:34.608 --> 37:36.109
[sighs]

575
37:41.698 --> 37:43.492
[sighs]

576
37:52.709 --> 37:54.419
[breathing heavily]

577
38:00.967 --> 38:01.968
[gasps]

578
38:24.199 --> 38:25.325
[grunts]

579
38:26.243 --> 38:28.203
[gasps, grunts]

580
38:33.750 --> 38:35.210
[gasps] Chris, hey!

581
38:39.714 --> 38:41.633
Chris. Chris!

582
38:43.593 --> 38:44.761
Chris.

583
38:50.183 --> 38:53.061
[coughing]

584
38:55.647 --> 38:56.648
Chris.

585
38:57.440 --> 38:58.441
You're awake.

586
39:01.361 --> 39:02.571
You're at the hospital.

587
39:04.698 --> 39:06.700
Hey! Don't push yourself. Just stay still.

588
39:06.783 --> 39:07.784
I'm okay.

589
39:09.369 --> 39:10.704
[sighs]

590
39:13.665 --> 39:16.585
How long have I been here?

591
39:17.169 --> 39:18.753
About 15 minutes.

592
39:20.005 --> 39:24.009
Seeing as you passed out, they suspected it's orthostatic hypotension

593
39:24.092 --> 39:26.011
rather than just anemia.

594
39:26.094 --> 39:27.762
They wanted to run more tests once you woke up--

595
39:27.846 --> 39:28.930
No.

596
39:30.265 --> 39:31.391
There's no need.

597
39:35.896 --> 39:36.897
Chris.

598
39:36.980 --> 39:38.607
Chris. Wait. Hold on.

599
39:41.443 --> 39:42.986
What's going on, huh?

600
39:48.783 --> 39:49.993
It's myasthenia gravis.

601
39:50.744 --> 39:52.370
Myasthenia gravis?

602
39:52.954 --> 39:54.289
I'm fine most of the time, but

603
39:55.373 --> 39:56.833
suddenly, I, uh…

604
39:58.043 --> 40:00.295
My whole body can become paralyzed.

605
40:00.378 --> 40:01.713
[gasping]

606
40:02.297 --> 40:03.882
It can't be cured here.

607
40:04.966 --> 40:06.092
Actually,

608
40:07.219 --> 40:08.220
not anywhere.

609
40:11.514 --> 40:12.557
Don't worry, my

610
40:13.892 --> 40:15.435
attacks are very rare.

611
40:16.269 --> 40:17.812
[sighs]

612
40:19.064 --> 40:20.065
Um…

613
40:24.861 --> 40:25.862
Ms. Seon.

614
40:28.323 --> 40:29.908
Please don't tell anyone about this.

615
40:30.492 --> 40:31.826
I'm counting on you.

616
40:34.537 --> 40:35.580
Please, I beg you.

617
40:37.249 --> 40:39.042
Just until the competition's over.

618
40:41.878 --> 40:42.921
[sighs]

619
41:10.073 --> 41:12.909
Gosh. There is more to pack than I expected.

620
41:12.993 --> 41:16.037
None of these are labeled, so I couldn't tell which was which.

621
41:16.538 --> 41:18.206
Tell Chris to double-check when he gets back.

622
41:18.290 --> 41:19.291
Okay.

623
41:19.374 --> 41:22.419
The balloon flower and wild grape enzyme extracts were really hard to find.

624
41:22.502 --> 41:23.920
They were tucked away in the back.

625
41:24.004 --> 41:25.547
Thank you.

626
41:27.173 --> 41:28.466
[Du-yeong sighs]

627
41:29.050 --> 41:32.887
Why did that shaman have to go on vacation now of all times?

628
41:32.971 --> 41:35.682
You couldn't find the right talisman around here?

629
41:36.433 --> 41:37.434
No.

630
41:37.517 --> 41:39.477
It was harder than I thought.

631
41:40.854 --> 41:43.148
-[Geon-woo] Hmm. -Song-yi, don't worry too much.

632
41:43.231 --> 41:44.774
You just have to get through tomorrow.

633
41:44.858 --> 41:48.570
What could possibly happen if you don't have your talisman for a little while?

634
41:48.653 --> 41:49.654
Right.

635
41:50.947 --> 41:52.198
[sighs]

636
41:52.282 --> 41:53.575
[door opens]

637
41:54.284 --> 41:55.702
Sounds like Chris is back.

638
41:55.785 --> 41:56.786
-Yeah. -Yeah.

639
41:59.581 --> 42:01.875
-Oh, Chris! -Oh, gosh. Are you okay?

640
42:02.542 --> 42:03.543
-[sighs] -[sighs]

641
42:06.338 --> 42:08.673
Ah. Well… Um…

642
42:09.799 --> 42:11.843
He slipped on the gym stairs and fell.

643
42:11.926 --> 42:13.053
That's what happened.

644
42:13.136 --> 42:14.179
On the stairs?

645
42:14.804 --> 42:16.806
-Are you badly hurt, Chris? -[Han] Mm-mmm.

646
42:16.890 --> 42:19.559
Not at all. I just twisted my ankle a little.

647
42:19.642 --> 42:20.685
It was pretty dark there.

648
42:24.647 --> 42:26.358
[chuckles] I'm fine, really.

649
42:26.441 --> 42:29.194
A hot compress, and it'll be better in no time.

650
42:29.861 --> 42:31.988
Well, let's go inside.

651
42:33.281 --> 42:34.366
Thank you.

652
42:36.284 --> 42:37.494
Oh. [grunts]

653
42:43.208 --> 42:44.709
[tense music playing]

654
42:44.793 --> 42:46.461
[Han] It's myasthenia gravis.

655
42:46.544 --> 42:48.671
It can't be cured here.

656
42:48.755 --> 42:50.757
Please don't tell anyone about this.

657
42:50.840 --> 42:51.841
I'm counting on you.

658
43:02.560 --> 43:05.021
What… What are you talking about?

659
43:05.730 --> 43:07.440
What about me and Chris K.?

660
43:08.108 --> 43:09.109
Oh…

661
43:11.027 --> 43:12.570
Did I put you on the spot?

662
43:13.446 --> 43:15.615
Woo-jin. I mean…

663
43:15.698 --> 43:16.825
What's gotten into you?

664
43:16.908 --> 43:19.077
I'm the director and he's a contestant.

665
43:19.160 --> 43:20.912
What else could there be between us?

666
43:21.830 --> 43:23.540
The director and a contestant?

667
43:24.040 --> 43:25.458
[chuckles]

668
43:26.167 --> 43:28.169
That doesn't seem like the right way to describe

669
43:28.253 --> 43:30.713
two people linking arms so affectionately.

670
43:34.050 --> 43:35.093
[sighs]

671
43:35.176 --> 43:36.636
No, that was just…

672
43:38.430 --> 43:39.722
[sighs]

673
43:42.308 --> 43:44.144
[sighs] You have it all wrong.

674
43:44.227 --> 43:46.229
[scoffs] If I have it all wrong,

675
43:47.063 --> 43:48.148
explain it to me.

676
43:52.986 --> 43:54.070
[sighs]

677
43:58.658 --> 43:59.659
I…

678
43:59.742 --> 44:00.827
[inhales sharply]

679
44:01.453 --> 44:04.080
I don't think I'm being overly sensitive.

680
44:08.209 --> 44:09.586
I think you know

681
44:11.171 --> 44:13.882
better than anyone how I feel about you.

682
44:15.300 --> 44:16.593
But

683
44:17.343 --> 44:18.344
sometimes…

684
44:21.514 --> 44:22.682
Sometimes I wonder…

685
44:25.810 --> 44:27.854
whether I was cast in a supporting role

686
44:28.605 --> 44:31.483
for Chris K.'s spectacular finale, or…

687
44:33.318 --> 44:34.903
whether Chris K. was cast

688
44:36.488 --> 44:40.533
as an obstacle I must overcome for a dramatic ending.

689
44:41.242 --> 44:42.619
[Jeong-won breathes shakily]

690
44:43.703 --> 44:44.704
I wonder

691
44:46.372 --> 44:48.708
which script you're working with.

692
44:53.463 --> 44:54.464
Of course…

693
44:55.798 --> 44:56.799
[inhales sharply]

694
44:57.550 --> 44:59.052
…we'd have to win today

695
45:01.012 --> 45:03.515
to get to that answer, I suppose.

696
45:04.933 --> 45:06.059
Otherwise,

697
45:07.101 --> 45:08.728
I'll never know the answer.

698
45:26.871 --> 45:28.581
[dramatic music playing]

699
45:37.966 --> 45:39.092
What an idiot.

700
45:42.762 --> 45:44.264
I shouldn't have said anything.

701
45:57.694 --> 45:59.696
[breathing heavily]

702
46:07.996 --> 46:09.872
[sighs]

703
46:16.879 --> 46:17.880
[grunts]

704
46:19.507 --> 46:21.843
[groaning]

705
46:24.304 --> 46:26.514
[upbeat music playing]

706
46:29.392 --> 46:32.604
[no audible dialogue]

707
46:39.819 --> 46:40.903
THE TABLE: K-CHEF 2026 CHAT ROOM

708
46:40.987 --> 46:43.281
[viewer] Wow, that's awesome. They're going to air the competition live?

709
46:43.364 --> 46:45.908
[viewer 2] So, they're airing it live? That's awesome.

710
46:46.534 --> 46:49.162
Your skin looks amazing today, ma'am.

711
46:49.245 --> 46:51.205
The makeup is going on beautifully.

712
46:52.248 --> 46:53.666
Really? Do I look okay?

713
46:53.750 --> 46:55.251
[chuckles]

714
46:55.335 --> 46:57.295
You look absolutely beautiful today, ma'am.

715
46:58.004 --> 46:59.589
[chuckles]

716
47:02.884 --> 47:06.220
By the way, Ms. Seon, are you feeling all right? You look pale.

717
47:07.138 --> 47:09.474
Oh. Oh, I'm fine.

718
47:10.141 --> 47:12.185
I just didn't sleep well last night.

719
47:12.810 --> 47:14.520
Mmm, I see. [chuckles]

720
47:16.147 --> 47:18.024
Oh, the broadcast is starting.

721
47:19.817 --> 47:21.569
There you are.

722
47:21.653 --> 47:22.654
Yeah.

723
47:23.821 --> 47:24.822
All set, Chairwoman?

724
47:24.906 --> 47:26.616
Yeah, almost.

725
47:26.699 --> 47:28.242
I'll be going now, Chairwoman.

726
47:29.827 --> 47:32.830
Why so soon? Are you going to wait in the broadcast truck?

727
47:32.914 --> 47:35.750
A senior colleague is directing the live broadcast.

728
47:35.833 --> 47:39.962
If I'm there, he'll probably feel like I'm watching over his shoulder.

729
47:40.046 --> 47:41.547
I'll sit in the audience.

730
47:41.631 --> 47:43.758
That is a good idea.

731
47:43.841 --> 47:45.718
You should relax and just enjoy the show for once.

732
47:45.802 --> 47:47.804
[chuckles] I will.

733
47:48.554 --> 47:49.555
[Hae-seon] Take care.

734
47:51.933 --> 47:56.062
[door opens, closes]

735
48:05.947 --> 48:07.573
I've really wanted to meet you.

736
48:07.657 --> 48:10.618
Seeing you in person, wow…

737
48:11.953 --> 48:14.122
You're really handsome.

738
48:14.789 --> 48:16.874
Oh, you're blinding me!

739
48:17.917 --> 48:19.919
[laughing]

740
48:20.002 --> 48:21.337
You can relax now.

741
48:21.421 --> 48:23.840
I only stopped by to wish you luck. [inhales deeply]

742
48:23.923 --> 48:24.924
We should

743
48:25.925 --> 48:28.177
definitely meet sometime.

744
48:28.886 --> 48:29.887
Well, then,

745
48:30.513 --> 48:32.390
I look forward to seeing your work.

746
48:33.766 --> 48:34.934
Seize the day.

747
48:41.190 --> 48:42.692
Let's go, Koo.

748
48:46.612 --> 48:48.156
[door closes]

749
48:48.239 --> 48:50.783
[Sang-hyeon] All right. We're starting the live countdown.

750
48:51.492 --> 48:53.453
Ten. Nine.

751
48:53.536 --> 48:54.829
Eight.

752
49:05.965 --> 49:08.551
THE TABLE: K-CHEF 2026

753
49:08.634 --> 49:11.095
It's the moment we've all been waiting for!

754
49:12.680 --> 49:16.100
The Table: K-Chef 2026 round 3 now begins.

755
49:16.184 --> 49:19.771
For the next two hours, we'll bring you a live cooking show

756
49:19.854 --> 49:23.065
unlike anything Korean TV has ever seen!

757
49:23.149 --> 49:25.359
-[audience cheering] -[applause]

758
49:40.917 --> 49:42.794
[monitor chiming]

759
49:42.877 --> 49:43.961
YOU ARE MY DESTINY

760
49:44.921 --> 49:45.922
That's it.

761
49:46.005 --> 49:48.549
"You are my destiny."

762
49:48.633 --> 49:52.094
As mentioned earlier in Part One, this round's challenge is

763
49:52.178 --> 49:54.263
to pair your dishes with Korean liquor.

764
49:54.347 --> 49:56.974
But which liquor will you be pairing your dishes with?

765
49:57.058 --> 49:59.769
Which liquor will be featured in this round?

766
49:59.852 --> 50:03.898
These questions must have plagued you for the last five days.

767
50:11.489 --> 50:16.118
Now tell me, what liquor do these puzzling clues point to exactly?

768
50:16.202 --> 50:20.122
Did the chefs seated back there figure it out during their

769
50:20.206 --> 50:23.042
past five days of preparation?

770
50:23.125 --> 50:29.048
And did they prepare a proper spread that pairs well with that liquor?

771
50:29.715 --> 50:35.763
As you all know, two teams joined forces to compete in this round.

772
50:35.847 --> 50:39.141
So, in other words, both teams in the losing group will be eliminated,

773
50:39.225 --> 50:41.561
not only one.

774
50:41.644 --> 50:44.814
And on top of that, we are live tonight.

775
50:44.897 --> 50:46.941
We are live.

776
50:47.525 --> 50:52.321
Chefs, with that said, I hope you'll give today's round everything you've got.

777
50:53.322 --> 50:58.494
Now then, what do these three clues point to for today's challenge?

778
50:59.704 --> 51:03.958
And now, the Korean liquor that these three clues point to!

779
51:04.041 --> 51:07.169
Drumroll, please.

780
51:07.879 --> 51:11.382
Let's reveal that liquor!

781
51:12.550 --> 51:17.722
Right now…

782
51:17.805 --> 51:19.265
Put up the photo.

783
51:21.559 --> 51:27.189
[Captain Cook] But before we do, why don't we take ourselves a short break?

784
51:27.273 --> 51:28.691
[laughing]

785
51:28.774 --> 51:29.775
Well, why not?

786
51:29.859 --> 51:32.570
It's better than a commercial break, isn't it?

787
51:32.653 --> 51:33.863
Come on.

788
51:33.946 --> 51:35.114
All right.

789
51:35.197 --> 51:39.285
Everyone, take a close look at the photo on the screen.

790
51:39.994 --> 51:45.791
Our production team went to great lengths to obtain these extremely rare photos.

791
51:45.875 --> 51:47.043
And

792
51:47.793 --> 51:52.256
they're childhood photos of the chefs that are gathered here today.

793
51:52.340 --> 51:55.426
[laughing] Oh, oh, oh!

794
51:55.509 --> 51:58.971
We weren't able to get photos of everyone, so don't be too nervous.

795
51:59.555 --> 52:01.599
Before we begin with the live show,

796
52:01.682 --> 52:04.143
we'd like to have you all play a little game

797
52:04.226 --> 52:06.520
to help loosen up a bit.

798
52:06.604 --> 52:08.022
[laughing]

799
52:08.105 --> 52:09.690
All right, everyone.

800
52:09.774 --> 52:11.400
Here's the first question.

801
52:14.487 --> 52:15.821
What is this?

802
52:16.781 --> 52:18.866
Was this segment in the original script?

803
52:18.950 --> 52:20.242
Uh, no.

804
52:20.952 --> 52:21.953
No, it wasn't.

805
52:22.036 --> 52:25.247
-Huh. -Something is off.

806
52:25.331 --> 52:27.541
[Captain Cook] The child in this photo

807
52:27.625 --> 52:31.671
is one of the head chefs here with us today in the competition.

808
52:31.754 --> 52:34.423
Well, this was taken before he started elementary school,

809
52:34.507 --> 52:36.467
so he must look quite different now.

810
52:36.550 --> 52:40.846
But that sharp nose and confident gaze slightly beneath the bowl cut

811
52:40.930 --> 52:45.393
seem to have the same direction today as they did back then.

812
52:45.476 --> 52:48.604
Now, take a closer look at the photo.

813
52:49.146 --> 52:53.943
Doesn't someone here resemble the child in the photo before you?

814
52:54.819 --> 52:58.406
All right, Chefs. Anyone want to take a little guess?

815
52:58.489 --> 52:59.699
I know!

816
52:59.782 --> 53:02.994
Oh! Chef Isabel may have an answer.

817
53:04.537 --> 53:07.289
Who is the child in this photo?

818
53:07.373 --> 53:09.291
Tell us, Isabel.

819
53:10.459 --> 53:12.378
Cha Woo-jin, uh, right?

820
53:17.341 --> 53:18.884
[Captain Cook] Chef Cha Woo-jin.

821
53:18.968 --> 53:20.511
With a bowl cut?

822
53:21.846 --> 53:25.433
Cha Woo-jin is correct!

823
53:25.516 --> 53:28.144
-[laughing] -[cheering]

824
53:31.022 --> 53:32.106
Whoo!

825
53:32.898 --> 53:35.568
Yes, the child in the photo is

826
53:35.651 --> 53:38.904
Cha Woo-jin, our wonderful chef.

827
53:39.739 --> 53:42.199
Here's the second photo, everyone.

828
53:42.283 --> 53:44.869
Please direct your attention to the screen.

829
53:49.165 --> 53:51.542
[dramatic music playing]

830
53:57.506 --> 53:59.133
[gasps]

831
53:59.717 --> 54:00.843
What is this?

832
54:02.970 --> 54:05.931
-[Captain Cook] Oh, ho, ho. -[breathing shakily]

833
54:06.015 --> 54:09.268
[Captain Cook] Is this one too difficult for you?

834
54:10.061 --> 54:13.773
No one seems quite ready to raise a hand, I see.

835
54:14.899 --> 54:17.777
Oh, from Bingsak, Chef Park Je-hyeon.

836
54:18.402 --> 54:19.570
Um…

837
54:20.321 --> 54:22.531
Joshua?

838
54:23.199 --> 54:24.617
[Captain Cook] Joshua

839
54:24.700 --> 54:26.744
is wrong!

840
54:26.827 --> 54:28.996
[laughing]

841
54:29.080 --> 54:31.499
Yes, from Golden Dragon, Chef Yang Ja-ryong.

842
54:31.582 --> 54:32.917
[inhales sharply]

843
54:34.001 --> 54:37.922
Eh, mmm…

844
54:38.506 --> 54:39.882
It's Chris!

845
54:39.965 --> 54:42.301
Isn't it? Chef Chris K.!

846
54:43.427 --> 54:45.471
[Captain Cook] Chris K.?

847
54:45.554 --> 54:47.890
Chris K.

848
54:47.973 --> 54:50.601
-is correct, Chef Yang Ja-ryong! -[cheering]

849
54:50.684 --> 54:52.436
[Captain Cook laughing]

850
54:53.145 --> 54:54.730
Yes.

851
54:54.814 --> 54:58.859
The child in this photo is, in fact, Chris K.

852
54:58.943 --> 55:00.820
[laughing]

853
55:03.739 --> 55:05.366
This can't be. [breathing shakily]

854
55:08.160 --> 55:09.161
[sighs]

855
55:20.339 --> 55:22.550
[Captain Cook] But here's something, Chris.

856
55:23.217 --> 55:25.970
According to what our production team found out,

857
55:26.053 --> 55:28.013
the man standing right next to you…

858
55:38.065 --> 55:40.401
turns out to be quite famous.

859
55:41.735 --> 55:42.820
That man

860
55:42.903 --> 55:45.990
is Kang San, the grandson of Master Kang Si-hu,

861
55:46.615 --> 55:48.701
royal head chef to Emperor Gojong

862
55:49.368 --> 55:51.203
of the Korean empire.

863
55:51.287 --> 55:53.289
[audience exclaiming]

864
55:57.710 --> 55:58.919
[Captain Cook] But, Chris,

865
55:59.503 --> 56:02.882
tell us why that man is standing beside you.

866
56:05.634 --> 56:06.635
Who is that man

867
56:07.720 --> 56:09.305
to you, Chris?

868
56:12.516 --> 56:14.935
Is there a chance that he…

869
56:19.565 --> 56:22.735
is your father, Chris?

870
56:33.204 --> 56:34.205
[gasps]

871
56:50.221 --> 56:51.222
Chris.

872
56:52.097 --> 56:54.558
Is that man up there your father?

873
56:58.896 --> 57:01.982
CANNOT ADDRESS HIS FATHER AS "FATHER."

874
57:10.491 --> 57:11.659
[gasps]

875
57:14.870 --> 57:15.871
That man…

876
57:24.964 --> 57:26.298
Kang San is…

877
57:28.634 --> 57:30.261
indeed my father.

878
57:30.344 --> 57:31.428
[gasps]

879
57:33.305 --> 57:35.516
[chuckles] Wow. [gasps]

880
57:35.599 --> 57:40.187
Wow, what a tearful family reunion I put together.

881
57:40.271 --> 57:43.524
[gasps] Congratulations, Hae-seon.

882
57:43.607 --> 57:46.360
[laughing]

883
57:50.322 --> 57:51.991
[breathing shakily]

884
58:00.374 --> 58:01.959
-[door opens] -Chairwoman Moon.

885
58:02.042 --> 58:03.043
Hae-seon!

886
58:05.129 --> 58:08.716
So, that man is your father, isn't he, Chris?

887
58:09.425 --> 58:10.718
Then, please…

888
58:12.761 --> 58:14.596
tell us, what is your…

889
58:15.889 --> 58:17.349
Korean name, Chris?

890
58:26.817 --> 58:27.818
Chris.

891
58:28.610 --> 58:30.654
Please tell us, what is your

892
58:32.448 --> 58:33.449
Korean name?

893
58:37.661 --> 58:38.662
[echoing] Chris.

894
58:40.622 --> 58:43.042
What is your Korean name?

895
58:45.711 --> 58:47.629
Please tell us, Chris.

896
58:49.048 --> 58:50.174
Chris.

897
58:52.426 --> 58:53.510
Chris?

898
58:58.807 --> 59:00.142
[emotional music playing]

899
59:17.534 --> 59:19.661
[breathing heavily]

900
59:47.564 --> 59:48.565
My name is…

901
59:51.985 --> 59:52.986
Kang Han.

902
59:56.740 --> 59:59.159
[pop song playing]

903
01:00:32.192 --> 01:00:34.153
-[Han] Have you forgotten? -[Captain Cook exclaims]

904
01:00:34.236 --> 01:00:36.405
Pyeongyeon led your father to his death. We have to beat them.

905
01:00:36.488 --> 01:00:38.574
Remember just two things in this round.

906
01:00:38.657 --> 01:00:40.617
Memory and imagination.

907
01:00:40.701 --> 01:00:42.786
What other surprises do you have in store?

908
01:00:43.495 --> 01:00:44.955
I can't do this, Chris.

909
01:00:45.581 --> 01:00:47.958
You have instinct and sensitivity.

910
01:00:48.041 --> 01:00:49.293
I know you do.

911
01:00:50.210 --> 01:00:52.296
You said that he could die.

912
01:00:53.172 --> 01:00:54.882
[Han] The owner of Famiglia…

913
01:00:54.965 --> 01:00:56.175
[Woo-jin] Come on. Wake up.

914
01:00:56.258 --> 01:00:59.261
-Hey, Chris! -[Han] …is neither me nor anyone else.

